---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const headings = [
  { id: 'getting-started', label: 'Getting started' },
  { id: 'development', label: 'Development' },
  { id: 'architecture', label: 'Architecture' },
  { id: 'pull-requests', label: 'Pull requests' },
  { id: 'reporting-issues', label: 'Reporting issues' },
  { id: 'code-style', label: 'Code style' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Contributing"
  description="Set up the ARC UI repo, regenerate the framework packages, and open a pull request or issue."
  activeSlug="contributing"
  headings={headings}
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Contributing' }]}
>
  <div class="contributing-page">
    <h1 class="page-title">Contributing</h1>
    <p class="page-desc">
      ARC UI is MIT-licensed. Bug reports and pull requests go to the GitHub repository.
    </p>

    <section id="getting-started">
      <h2 class="docs-heading">Getting started</h2>
      <arc-divider align="left" variant="line-gradient" style="max-width:48px;margin-bottom:var(--space-md)"></arc-divider>
      <p class="docs-text">Prerequisites:</p>
      <ul class="docs-list">
        <li><strong>Node.js 24+</strong> (LTS)</li>
        <li><strong>pnpm 10+</strong></li>
        <li>Git</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="docs-code"><arc-code-block language="bash" code="git clone https://github.com/Arclight-Digital/arc-ui.git
cd arc-ui
pnpm install"></arc-code-block></div>
      <p class="docs-text">
        The <code>packageManager</code> field pins the pnpm version. Use
        <strong>pnpm</strong> for every command in the repo.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="development">
      <h2 class="docs-heading">Development</h2>
      <arc-divider align="left" variant="line-gradient" style="max-width:48px;margin-bottom:var(--space-md)"></arc-divider>
      <p class="docs-text">
        Work on components in the docs site. Start it with:
      </p>
      <div class="docs-code"><arc-code-block language="bash" code="pnpm dev"></arc-code-block></div>
      <p class="docs-text">
        After editing Web Component source in <code>packages/web-components/src/</code> or tokens in
        <code>shared/tokens.js</code>, regenerate everything (framework wrappers, HTML examples, and CSS):
      </p>
      <div class="docs-code"><arc-code-block language="bash" code="pnpm generate"></arc-code-block></div>
      <arc-alert variant="warning">
        Don't hand-edit the framework packages (<code>packages/react/</code>,
        <code>vue/</code>, <code>svelte/</code>, <code>angular/</code>, <code>solid/</code>,
        <code>preact/</code>), <code>packages/html/css/</code>, or
        <code>shared/base.css</code>. <code>pnpm generate</code> writes them and overwrites
        your edits.
      </arc-alert>
      <p class="docs-text">
        Bump versions with this script, which updates every package at once. Don't edit
        <code>package.json</code> versions by hand.
      </p>
      <div class="docs-code"><arc-code-block language="bash" code="pnpm bump-versions <version>"></arc-code-block></div>
    </section>

    <section id="architecture">
      <h2 class="docs-heading">Architecture</h2>
      <arc-divider align="left" variant="line-gradient" style="max-width:48px;margin-bottom:var(--space-md)"></arc-divider>
      <p class="docs-text">
        ARC UI is a monorepo. The Lit web components are the source, and Prism, a custom code
        generator, reads them and writes a wrapper package for each framework.
      </p>
      <p class="docs-text">Components are organized into seven tiers:</p>
      <ul class="docs-list">
        <li><strong>Layout</strong>: Page scaffolding (AppShell, Container, PageLayout)</li>
        <li><strong>Navigation</strong>: Menus, links, tabs, breadcrumbs</li>
        <li><strong>Content</strong>: Cards, avatars, icons, carousels</li>
        <li><strong>Data</strong>: Tables, lists, badges, meters, stats, timelines</li>
        <li><strong>Typography</strong>: Code blocks, markdown, text, kbd</li>
        <li><strong>Input</strong>: Buttons, forms, selects, sliders</li>
        <li><strong>Feedback</strong>: Dialogs, toasts, tooltips</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="docs-text">
        Design tokens are defined in <code>shared/tokens.js</code>, and
        <code>pnpm generate</code> writes <code>shared/base.css</code> from it.
        Compound tokens must use <code>var()</code> references so consumers can override
        just the base tokens.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="pull-requests">
      <h2 class="docs-heading">Pull requests</h2>
      <arc-divider align="left" variant="line-gradient" style="max-width:48px;margin-bottom:var(--space-md)"></arc-divider>
      <ol class="docs-list">
        <li>Fork the repository and create a feature branch from <code>main</code></li>
        <li>Make your changes to the Web Component source</li>
        <li>Run <code>pnpm generate</code> to regenerate wrappers and CSS</li>
        <li>Run <code>pnpm lint</code> and <code>pnpm format:check</code></li>
        <li>Test your changes in the docs site (<code>pnpm dev</code>)</li>
        <li>Open a pull request describing the change</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="reporting-issues">
      <h2 class="docs-heading">Reporting issues</h2>
      <arc-divider align="left" variant="line-gradient" style="max-width:48px;margin-bottom:var(--space-md)"></arc-divider>
      <p class="docs-text">
        Open an issue on
        <a href="https://github.com/Arclight-Digital/arc-ui/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        with:
      </p>
      <ul class="docs-list">
        <li>Steps to reproduce (for bugs)</li>
        <li>Expected and actual behavior</li>
        <li>Browser and OS version</li>
        <li>A minimal reproduction if possible</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="code-style">
      <h2 class="docs-heading">Code style</h2>
      <arc-divider align="left" variant="line-gradient" style="max-width:48px;margin-bottom:var(--space-md)"></arc-divider>
      <ul class="docs-list">
        <li>Web Components are plain JavaScript (no TypeScript build step)</li>
        <li>Use <code>static properties</code> instead of decorators</li>
        <li>Follow existing naming: <code>arc-component-name</code> for tags, <code>ArcComponentName</code> for classes</li>
        <li>All components import <code>tokenStyles</code> from <code>../shared-styles.js</code></li>
        <li>Use <code>var(--token-name)</code> for all colors, spacing, and typography</li>
        <li>Clean up event listeners in <code>disconnectedCallback()</code></li>
        <li>Make interactive components work from the keyboard</li>
        <li>Run <code>pnpm format</code> before committing</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="see-also">
      <h2 class="docs-heading">See also</h2>
      <arc-divider align="left" variant="line-gradient" style="max-width:48px;margin-bottom:var(--space-md)"></arc-divider>
      <ul class="see-also__list">
        <li><a href="/docs/getting-started">Getting started</a>: installation and setup</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/accessibility">Accessibility</a>: what the components handle and how they're audited</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/tokens">Tokens</a>: design token reference</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
